8a. **Populate-pool (mandatory when Redis L2 enabled):** only **`populate-pool`** workers (`sync_timedb:worker:populate-pool`, `pool_kind=populate-pool`) may execute `populate_archive_members_redis` scan_fn / `_stream_compressed_archive_members` / `_populate_redis_members_from_*` when Redis L2 is enabled. **Ingest-pool** and **archive-pool** callers use `request_archive_members_populate_and_wait` (enqueue + Redis wait only). **Production fatal class:** any **`[sync_timedb:worker:ingest-pool] … sealed archive member stream failed`** (often under **`IngestPerFileTimeoutError` / SIGALRM**) is a contract violation — ingest must never fall through to local sealed scan when Redis L2 is enabled (including cold Redis, populate-pool down, degraded, or timeout paths). When populate-pool controller is None in spawn workers (normal) or MainThread pool is briefly down, ingest/archive must **enqueue** Redis populate jobs and wait within `populate_max_seconds` — **never** call `execute_archive_members_populate_for_canonical` / sealed stream, and **never** map refuse-stream to immediate MainThread L2 `sys.exit(1)`. MainThread may `reap_and_restart` then enqueue; `is_populate_pool_unavailable_error` / exit helper treat refuse-stream as recoverable. `execute_…` remains **forbidden on ingest-pool**. Populate wait paths (`wait_for_complete_members`, `wait_for_member_match` on populate lock) must pass **`respect_ingest_deadline=False`** — never consult per-file ingest ContextVar / `IngestArchiveLookupBudgetExceededError` during populate wait. **On ingest-pool workers inside `_run_ingest_timed`, populate wait must also suspend per-file `SIGALRM` (`suspend_ingest_sigalrm_for_populate_wait`) and extend the monotonic ingest deadline by wait wall time** — populate wait remains bounded by populate stall/max limits only, not `sync_ingest_per_file_timeout_s`. INI: `sync_archive_members_populate_pool_processes` (default **4**). Inline tests without a running pool may fall back to `execute_archive_members_populate_for_canonical` (temporarily sets `pool_kind=populate-pool`) **only when pool_kind is unset / MainThread**. **Populate-pool liveness:** `PopulatePoolController.stop` must **always `join`** dead workers (zombies have `is_alive()==False` but still need reap); chunk-boundary **`reap_and_restart`** replaces dead workers up to the configured count. **Wait identity drift:** waiters pass `canonical=` and **re-resolve** `_daily_archive_members_cache_key` each poll so concurrent tar append (T1→T2 fingerprint) succeeds when the **current** identity is fully warm (`complete=1`, non-empty HASH). Log **`INFO: populate_wait identity_drift`** at most **once per 120s per calendar day** (`suppressed_n=` on resume); do not log every poll during append. **Incomplete after lock release (`hlen==0`):** clear stale incomplete/degraded keys and **re-enqueue** within `sync_archive_members_redis_populate_max_seconds` (default **7200**) when **`daily_archive_populate_source_exists`** — **do not** re-enqueue when no tar and no sealed (return **`{}`**); stale incomplete logs rate-limited per day. **Lock-held stall with alive owner:** do **not** fatal on the first `populate_stall_seconds` when owner PID is alive and wait is still within `populate_max_seconds` (heartbeat may briefly fail). Do **not** fatal on the first empty-incomplete stall when max_seconds > 0. **Imap stall ordering:** `_ingest_stall_defer_state` must prefer **`redis_populate_active`** over **`idle_pool_ghost_inflight`** (workers in `hrtimer_nanosleep` during Redis wait look idle). Regression: `test_ingest_worker_never_streams_sealed_on_cold_redis`, `test_ingest_worker_never_streams_sealed_when_populate_pool_down`, `test_populate_lock_held_stall_recoverable_within_max_seconds`, `test_ingest_stall_defer_redis_populate_before_idle_ghost`, `test_populate_wait_succeeds_when_tar_identity_drifts_to_warm_key`, `test_incomplete_after_lock_release_reenqueues_before_fatal`, `test_request_populate_no_wait_when_no_daily_a