15a. **Normal-path zombie reap (mandatory):** fatal teardown alone is insufficient when `maxtasksperchild>0` or populate-pool workers die mid-run. **`abort_if_pool_workers_dead` healthy recycle** (`exitcode 0` or supervisor **`retire_pool_worker_pid`** SIGTERM when tracked, replacements keeping pace) must call **`reap_pool_worker_pids`** and **`reap_zombie_children_of_self`** every check and **must not** raise exit **137** — log **`INFO: pool worker recycle in progress`** once per dead PID; **`WARN: pool worker recycle slow`** after **`sync_pool_worker_recycle_grace_seconds`** (default **60**). A global grace **poll** counter across consecutive different PIDs is forbidden (hpcperfstats03: grace 1/2 → 2/2 → fatal on third PID at 15/16 alive). Healthy recycle compares alive count against **`expected_pool_workers`** (ingest **`sync_ingest_pool_processes`**) when materialized workers lag process cap during spawn (July-08: **20/21** tolerated after **23/24** polls); fatal **`likely_cause=recycle_stuck`** (not bare **`recycle`**) when replacement truly stalls, with **`ERROR: pool worker recycle gate rejected:`** metrics. Shipped default **`sync_ingest_pool_maxtasksperchild=0`**: supervisor **`failure_reap` / `rss_reap`** retire after imap result collection uses the same grace contract — path size alone never retires; **never supervisor-retire on `outcome=db_skip`** except RSS. **Post-retire maintenance (mandatory when `maxtasks=0`):** after each supervisor **`retire_pool_worker_pid`**, call **`maintain_ingest_pool_after_supervisor_retire`** — reap zombies, log **`WARN: ingest pool replacement lagging`** when materialized workers lag **`expected_pool_workers`**, **refuse further retire/swap while `gap>0`**, and only run **`probe_ingest_pool_dispatch` when `pool_workers_all_idle`** (busy pool → **`INFO: post_retire_maintenance skip_probe reason=workers_busy`**; coalesce successive busy maintains within ~5s → **`INFO: post_retire_maintenance coalesced reason=workers_busy`**)