bie_children_of_self`** (PID-specific waitpid for `/proc` state-`Z` children of `os.getpid()` — **not** `waitpid(-1)`), and **`populate_pool_controller.reap_and_restart`**. **Mid-chunk:** `_maybe_reap_supervisor_pool_children_throttled` (default **60s**) from **`on_stall_poll`**, **`pending rescan done`**, and **`_maybe_log_ingest_stall_watchdog`** backstops long imap gaps. **`warn_unreaped_zombie_children`** logs WARN when zombies remain after any reap attempt. Regression: `test_terminate_pool_bounded_abandon_skips_blocking_terminate`, `test_recover_wall_raises_stall_not_soft_hang`, `test_recover_does_not_clear_pending_before_new_pool_ready`, `test_no_giant_reap_on_db_skip`, `test_maintain_ingest_pool_proactive_swap_abandons_old_pool`, `test_abort_recycle_consecutive_different_pids_no_fatal`, `test_abort_recycle_20_of_21_alive_no_fatal`, `test_abort_recycle_24_cap_20_alive_one_dead_no_fatal`, `test_abort_recycle_22_pool_19_alive_three_dead_no_fatal`, `test_abort_recycle_spawn_gap_raw_pool_len_no_fatal`, `test_abort_recycle_grace_reaps_dead_worker_pids`, `test_abort_recycle_grace_reaps_zombie_children`, `test_reap_zombie_children_of_self_waitpids_state_z`, `test_reap_supervisor_pool_children_throttled`, `test_ingest_stall_poll_triggers_throttled_reap`, `test_populate_pool_stop_joins_dead_processes`, `test_populate_pool_reap_waitpids_dead_worker`, `test_supervisor_retire_sigterm_counts_as_healthy_recycle`, `test_terminate_pool_bounded_kill_workers_first_before_terminate`, `test_probe_ingest_pool_dispatch_success_and_failure`, `test_maintain_ingest_pool_after_supervisor_retire_noop_when_maxtasks_positive`, `test_full_redispatch_thrash_triggers_immediate_recover_same_round`.
16. **Tar mutation invalidation:** mutating changes to a daily archive must refresh member caches. **`tar_append` success** calls **`merge_appended_members_into_redis`** (HSET new members, keep `complete=1`) + L1 merge — **not** full **`invalidate_after_daily_tar_mutation`** unless merge fails/disabled. **`archive_append_inflight`** Redis key is set **first** in **`_archive_stats_files_body`** (before pre-append member lookup) for the calendar day for the full job (cleared in `finally`) so **other** populate winners defer full tar scans until job-end merge; archive-pool pre-append lookup uses **`archive_pre_append_member_lookup_context`** so the same job does not self-defer. **`archive_finalize`** must **skip** invalidate (and synchronous hook prewarm) when the append worker reports **`ArchiveAppendOutcome.skip_finalize_invalidate`** (Redis merge warm or worker already invalidated on merge failure). When finalize invalidate is still required, the invalidation hook must **defer** synchronous prewarm to the **chunk boundary** (`deferred_archive_finalize_prewarm_days` flush), coalesced per calendar day. **Full invalidation** remains required for: seal, dedupe rewrite, identity change, bootstrap append when merge unavailable, and **`archive_finalize`** when append did not keep Redis warm. Log `INFO: tar_append redis merge day=… members=N` on merge path; `INFO: archive_finalize skip invalidate day=… reason=redis_merge_warm`.
17. **Archive pool append Redis parity:** **`_archive_stats_files_body`** (archive pool workers) must resolve **`existing_members`** via **`get_existing_archive_members_for_daily_archive(canonical)`** when Redis L2 is enabled — same Redis-first path as ingest duplicate-check. **Forbidden:** calling **`get_existing_archive_members(tar)`** (full sibling **`.tar`** scan under **`file_read_lock`**) when Redis is fully warm (`complete=1`, non-empty HASH). Log **`archive_job_begin … members_source=redis|tar_scan`** and **`archive_job_done elapsed_s=…`** for operator stall diagnosis. Post-recovery and post-corrupt-restore member lookups use the same helper. Archive spawn pool always uses hardcoded **`maxtasksperchild=1`** (independent of ingest INI); append workers recycle after every task without supervisor failure retire.
18. **Per-file state re-entrancy:** supervisor **`file_states`** may re-enter ingest while raw remains on disk (checkpoint restore → **`ARCHIVED`**, pending rescan) or when archive dispatch replays deferred paths. **`_transition_file_state`** must allow **`ARCHIVE_QUEUED→WRITTEN`** and **`ARCHIVED→WRITTEN`** on db-complete / handoff re-ingest, and treat **`ARCHIVED→ARCHIVE_QUEUED`** as an idempotent no-op (path stays **`ARCHIVED`**). These are expected overlap paths — not **`Invalid sync_timedb file state transition`** errors. See **`sync-timedb-db-before-archive-contract.mdc`** (db-complete fast path) and **`sync-timedb-persistence-contract.mdc`** (checkpoint restore).

